ugh."
>>=20
>> This works because of the specificity of {lo} (being completely general,=
 one of its uses is as a specific gadri; go figure).  As you said, {lo klam=
a} now refers to the contextually appropriate goer(s) we were just speaking=
 of.  But the clear way to say that you're not among them would probably be=
 {mi na cmima lo'i klama}, which of course relies on the same contextual ap=
propriateness, but I think is clearer in the sense of saying that of this s=
et of goers, you are not a member.
